# CDL
#
# CDL, the netlist that layout-versus-schematic checks compare against: a
# SPICE netlist of connectivity only. Written in our own words from general
# knowledge of the format; no LVS tool was run against it.
# Lines marked "assumed" are the ones that knowledge does not settle.
#
# CDL has subcircuits, instances with `/` before the subcircuit name, the
# primitive devices, parameters, globals and includes. It has no sources, no
# analyses and no simulator controls. `$` starts a trailing comment, which
# is also where CDL keeps its annotations (`$[model]`, `$X=...`): they are
# carried over as comments. `*.PININFO`, `*.BIPOLAR` and the other `*.`
# lines are comments to a simulator and are carried over the same way.

dialect cdl

lexer
  case      insensitive
  # The first line is the title, written as a comment (assumed: CDL files
  # start with a `*` header, and LVS tools read nothing on that line).
  title     yes "* "
  comment   line "*"
  annotation "*@"          # a line a tool reads (cktImg's `*@ order m1 m2`), whole, in its scope
  comment   tail "$"                               # assumed: `$` ends the line's netlist and starts its annotations
  continue  lead "+"
  parens    space
  expr      "'" "'"                              # assumed
  values    idents
  # assumed: the SPICE letters, and units after them ignored, as in the
  # SPICE the CDL is written from; an LVS tool may read fewer (no a, no t).
  scale     meg=6 t=12 g=9 k=3 m=-3 u=-6 n=-9 p=-12 f=-15 a=-18
  units     ignore
  end       ".end"
end

block subckt
  open   ".subckt" name ports* {...params} -inline      # params on the header: assumed
  close  ".ends" [name]
end

rule  param     = ".param" {...params}
rule  global    = ".global" nodes+
rule  include   = ".include" path
read  include   = ".inc" path

rule  resistor  = name~"R" pos neg r {...params}
rule  capacitor = name~"C" pos neg c {...params}
rule  inductor  = name~"L" pos neg l {...params}
# assumed: the area of a diode and a BJT as a bare value, as in SPICE.
rule  diode     = name~"D" pos neg master [area] { area=area ...params? }
rule  bjt       = name~"Q" c b e [s] master [area] { area=area ...params? }
rule  mosfet    = name~"M" d g s b master {...params}
rule  jfet      = name~"J" d g s master [area] {...params}
# assumed: `/` before the master is written, and read with or without it.
rule  instance  = name~"X" nodes+ "/" master {...params}
read  instance  = name~"X" nodes+ master {...params}

no vsource   : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no isource   : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no bsource   : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no vcvs      : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no vccs      : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no cccs      : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no ccvs      : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no mutual    : CDL has no coupled inductors
no vswitch   : CDL has no switches
no cswitch   : CDL has no switches
no tline     : CDL has no transmission lines
no mesfet    : CDL has no MESFET element
no device    : CDL has no Verilog-A instances; a device is named by its model or subcircuit
no hdl       : CDL cannot load Verilog-A
no model     : CDL names device models but does not define them; LVS takes them from the rule deck
no func      : CDL has no user-defined functions
no lib       : CDL has no library sections
no libsection : CDL has no library sections
no cond_if   : CDL has no conditional blocks
no cond_elif : CDL has no conditional blocks
no cond_else : CDL has no conditional blocks
no options   : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no options
no save      : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no outputs
no print     : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no outputs
no ic        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no initial conditions
no nodeset   : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no initial conditions
no measure   : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no measurements
no op        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no dc        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no ac        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no tran      : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no noise     : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no tf        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no pz        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no sens      : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no disto     : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no four      : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no hb        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no sp        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no pss       : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no stb       : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no xspice : CDL has no XSPICE code models
# analyses (b3)
no pac        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no pnoise     : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no pxf        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no psp        : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no xf         : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no dcmatch    : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no trannoise  : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no phasenoise : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no envelope   : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no qpss       : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
# devices and outputs (b4)
no lossyline : CDL has no transmission lines
no ctlsrc  : CDL describes connectivity for LVS; it has no sources
no relay   : CDL has no switches
no simctl  : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no commands

# statistics
# A parameter of the netlist varies through agauss(), gauss(), aunif() or unif() in its
# definition; a statistics block's process variations are written that way
# when the varied parameter is defined in the same file.
no statistics : CDL has no statistics block; a parameter varies through agauss(), gauss(), aunif() or unif() in its definition
no statgroup : CDL has no statistics block; a parameter varies through agauss(), gauss(), aunif() or unif() in its definition
no vary : CDL has no statistics block; a parameter varies through agauss(), gauss(), aunif() or unif() in its definition
no correlate : CDL has no statement that correlates two random parameters
no montecarlo : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
# A library file has no wrapper around its sections; the name is carried
# as a comment.
block library
  open   "*" "library" name
  close  "*" "endlibrary"
end
caveat library name : CDL has no library wrapper around its sections; it is written as a comment
caveat subckt inline : CDL has no inline subcircuits; the subcircuit is written as an ordinary one, so the devices in it are named one level deeper

# assumed: the functions a parameter expression may use are SPICE's; what
# an LVS tool evaluates in a parameter is not settled.
functions
  same abs min max sqrt exp pow pwr floor ceil int sgn sin cos tan asin acos atan sinh cosh tanh
  ln    = log
  log10 = log10
end

operators
  pow "**" "^"                                   # assumed
end

# sweeps
no step : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no data : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no data tables
# alter (c2)
no alter : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses to rerun
no pattern : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no sources of patterns
no fft : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses or outputs
no optimize : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck; it has no analyses
no script : CDL is a netlist, not a simulation deck
no csparam : only a control script reads a .csparam vector, and cdl has none
no native : the statement is another dialect's own, which no kind holds; only that dialect writes it
no embed : VACASK embeds a file (a post-processing script) in the netlist; this dialect has no such statement, so save the file next to the netlist
